modpro workflow summary

basic architecture:
NiFi → monday/thursday manifests deposited on cron → monitor script triggers snakemake pipes → Snakemake Mondays pipeline (OpenFold3)
Snakemake Thursdays pipeline (Rosetta/QC) → Glyc/Epitope/SD data
→ results/logging_qc + results/final
→ NiFi → HDFS

Mondays/OpenFold3 pipeline:
1. NiFi pulls variant_hash + aa_seq CSV data on mondays from refsys
2. Groovy script converts CSV rows into FASTA-ish manifests:
   >variant_hash
   AA_SEQUENCE
3. Manifest written to manifests/*.csv
4. monitor_manifests.py watches for new .csv manifests
5. Trigger Snakefile-mondays
6. split_manifest checkpoint:
   - creates one FASTA per variant
   - writes variants.json
7. create msa_config.json per variant
8. run OpenFold3 MSA Snakefile
   - 2 concurrent MSA jobs
9. create query.json
10. run OpenFold3 inference
   - 1 concurrent inference job <must be run on scbs-vsdb-01 due to gpu constraint>
11. outputs:
   results/<manifest>/openfold3/
   results/<manifest>/logs/

random notes:
- OpenFold3 MSA Snakefile path:
  /scicomp/groups/modpro/openfold3/openfold-3/scripts/snakemake_msa/MSA_Snakefile
- all logs centralized under:
  results/<manifest>/logs/
- failure emails sent to qxa4@cdc.gov
- monitor exits on failure

Thursdays/Rosetta pipeline:
Nifi SQL pull from protein_modeling.logging_qc where variant_hash status is OF3_SUCCESS and not PUBLISHED
publishes a list of pdb names in manifests/*.tsv file
triggers the Snakefile-thursdays run from monitor_manifests.py

Thursdays snake job workflow
1. extract chain A and remove HA2
2. per-residue pLDDT and energy score extraction
3. Rosetta scoring/scripts
4. per-residue energetics
5. CA RMSD + MaxSub vs subtype reference
6. Rosetta relax
7. Pocket relax
8. qualitative metrics
9. choose best model by energy/RMSD
10. glyc/epitope/structural metrics
11. write outputs:
    results/logging_qc/
    results/final/
12. NiFi posts to HDFS

